
---
import LiquidCursor from '../components/LiquidCursor.astro';
import MusicPlayer from '../components/MusicPlayer.astro';
import ThemeToggle from '../components/ThemeToggle.astro';
import { ClientRouter } from 'astro:transitions';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <ClientRouter />
    <title>About — Turath</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles/global.css" />

    <style>
      header nav .logo {
        display: inline-flex;
        align-items: center;
        text-decoration: none;
      }

      header nav .site-logo {
        display: block;
        width: 57.6px;
        height: auto;
        max-width: 100%;
        object-fit: contain;
      }

      @media (max-width: 600px) {
        header nav .site-logo {
          width: 50.4px;
        }
      }
    </style>
  </head>

  <body>
    <LiquidCursor />
    <MusicPlayer />

    <header>
      <nav>
        <a href="/" class="logo" aria-label="Turath homepage">
          <img
            src="/images/logo.jpg"
            alt="Turath logo"
            class="site-logo"
          />
        </a>

        <div class="nav-links">
  <a href="/">Home</a>
  <a href="/about">About</a>
  <ThemeToggle />
</div>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <main>
      <article class="post-article">
        <h1>About Turath</h1>

        <p>
          Turath (Arabic تُراث) literally means heritage, tradition, and culture.
        </p>

        <p>
          The word comes from the Arabic root w-r-th (وَرث), meaning “to inherit”
          or “to receive as a legacy.” Over time, its meaning grew beyond material
          inheritance to represent the cultural, intellectual, and spiritual legacies
          passed from one generation to the next — language, art, customs, stories,
          beliefs, knowledge, and traditions.
        </p>

        <p>
          Turath originally began as an idea for a clothing brand: a way to display
          culture, art, and expression while creating a voice for people and
          communities whose stories are often overlooked, misunderstood, or unheard.
        </p>

        <p>
          The cultures intended to shape Turath include Congo, Iran, Algeria,
          Palestine, Sudan, Lebanon, Kurdistan, Iraq, Ethiopia, Afghanistan,
          South Africa, Somalia, Yemen, Haiti, and many others. These places represent
          incredibly rich and diverse histories — cultures shaped by faith, migration,
          creativity, colonialism, war, struggle, resilience, oppression, resistance,
          and survival.
        </p>

        <p>The idea for Turath began with myself and Leen.</p>

        <p>
          Leen was, and remains, one of the dearest people to my soul. She was my
          sister in everything but blood, my friend, and a divine expression of art,
          humour, feeling, elegance, and strength. She was a fighter — someone whose
          presence carried a warmth and spirit that is difficult to put into words.
        </p>

        <p>
          On October 29th, Leen’s life was cut short in Gaza when an Israeli missile
          struck the building where she and her family were residing. Leen, alongside
          her sister Sara, her brother Ibrahim, and her mother Enas, did not survive.
        </p>

        <p>
          There are some losses that change the shape of your life. For me, this was
          the biggest one.
        </p>

        <p>Turath is dedicated to Leen, Sara, Ibrahim, and Enas.</p>

        <p>
          What began as an idea between two people became something I now carry
          forward alone, but never without her. Turath was one of Leen’s last wishes
          for me — and fulfilling it is more than a project or a creative pursuit.
          It is a promise.
        </p>

        <p>
          Turath is a collection of ideas, stories, and perspectives across different
          subgenres of art, ranging from music, photography, creative directing,
          athletes, clothing brands, visual artists, entrepreneurs, business owners,
          music producers, and many more creatives.
        </p>
      </article>
    </main>

    <footer>
      <p>&copy; {new Date().getFullYear()} Turath. All rights reserved.</p>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
